al. However, establishing the pawn structure first is usually preferred when the opponent allows it.\n\nReason: Black\'s move 1... a5 is passive and ignores the battle for the center. By playing d2-d4, White establishes a dominant pawn duo in the center (e4 and d4). This maximizes White\'s control of the board, opens lines for the Queen and dark-squared Bishop, and punishes Black\'s strategic error.\n\nAnswer: P: d2-d4'}
